---
description: Never attribute the agent on the user's commits, pushes, or PRs
alwaysApply: true
---

# No agent attribution

The user's git history, commit messages, and pull requests are theirs alone.

- Never add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, `Reviewed-by`, or any other trailer that names the agent, Cursor, or a model.
- Never set the commit author, committer, or pusher to the agent. Leave `user.name` and `user.email` untouched.
- If a hook or tool injects such a trailer, remove it before the commit or push is finished.
- This applies to every repository, not only this one.
